CAT = "dkmcJunctions"; SEG = "JNC"
# Afsnit 7.10 to 7.15: traffic-calmed areas, approaching junctions, straight on, right and left turns, roundabouts.
Q = [
("You ride straight on through a junction. Who is most often the other party in a motorcycle crash there?",
 "Oncoming traffic turning left", ["The traffic right behind you", "Pedestrians on the corner", "Cyclists turning right"],
 "In junctions the other party is above all an oncoming vehicle turning left in front of the motorcyclist, then traffic from the right turning left or going straight on."),
("You approach a junction on your motorcycle. Why might a waiting driver not register you?",
 "You look small and far off", ["Your lights are too bright", "You always ride too slowly", "You are usually in a bus lane"],
 "A motorcycle fills less of the traffic picture than a car and is easily mistaken for a slower moped, so drivers misjudge both its presence and its speed."),
("Approaching a junction where a car waits to pull out, what should you do?",
 "Slow down and cover the brakes", ["Keep your speed and hold the horn", "Accelerate to clear it quickly", "Pass close behind the car"],
 "Expect that the driver may not have seen you. Slow down, keep your hand and foot ready on the brakes and make sure the driver has noticed you."),
("At a junction with a poor view to one side, which traffic do you tend to overlook?",
 "The side with a good view", ["Traffic from the poor-view side", "The traffic right behind you", "Traffic on a cycle track"],
 "Where the view is poor to one side, there is a tendency to overlook traffic coming from the side where the view is good."),
("You must stop at a junction ahead. What is the right way to slow down on a motorcycle?",
 "Ease off early, declutch late", ["Declutch early and coast", "Brake hard at the last moment", "Change into neutral early"],
 "Close the throttle in good time and, if needed, pull in the clutch only just before you stop. Plan stops early instead of braking hard at the end."),
("On a road with two lanes your way and no lane arrows, which lane do you choose before turning right?",
 "The lane furthest right", ["The lane furthest left", "Either lane", "The lane with less traffic"],
 "Without lane arrows, take the lane furthest to the right before a right turn and the lane furthest to the left before a left turn."),
("You turn left at a junction with traffic lights on an ordinary green light. What is a common mistake?",
 "Treating green as a free path", ["Waiting at the stop line", "Signalling before the junction", "Looking at the lights"],
 "A plain green light does not give you a free path to turn left. Riders who watch only the lights may overlook oncoming traffic going straight on, which they must give way to."),
("You come to a junction where the traffic lights are out of order and there are no give-way markings. Which rule applies?",
 "The right-hand rule", ["The larger road goes first", "Motorcycles go first", "Straight-on traffic goes first"],
 "If the lights do not work, follow any unconditional give-way markings; if there are none, the right-hand rule applies."),
("What does the Main road sign (B 16) tell you?",
 "Crossing traffic must give way", ["You must give way to the right", "The speed limit is 80 km/h", "Motorcycles are banned"],
 "The Main road sign shows that crossing traffic has an unconditional duty to give way, unless markings on the main road show otherwise."),
("You wait in the exposed space in the middle of a large junction to turn left, and the light changes. What tendency should you resist?",
 "Rushing the turn carelessly", ["Checking your mirrors", "Watching oncoming traffic", "Looking for pedestrians"],
 "Discomfort at the exposed waiting place in a big junction, or fear of being in the way when the light changes, can make riders finish the left turn carelessly. Make sure the junction is clear first."),
("While turning in a junction, what should you avoid doing with your eyes?",
 "Staring at other road users", ["Looking where you will go", "Checking the road surface", "Glancing at both your mirrors"],
 "After the necessary check, do not keep your eyes on other road users for long but let them go where you are going; you tend to steer where you look."),
("You turn right on a green right arrow. Which road users may still cross in front of you?",
 "Cyclists running a red", ["Lorries from the left", "Trams from behind", "Cars from the left on red"],
 "Watch for cyclists and moped riders going straight on despite a red cyclist signal while you have a green right arrow."),
("When you turn right on a motorcycle, from where can the other parties in a crash come?",
 "Almost any direction", ["Only from behind", "Only from the left", "Only from the cycle track"],
 "Motorcyclists turning right meet other parties from almost every direction, especially oncoming cars on the road being turned into."),
("Compared with other road users, how often are motorcyclists in crashes while turning left in junctions?",
 "Relatively rarely", ["More often than anyone", "Exactly as often as cars", "Only in roundabouts"],
 "Relatively few motorcycle crashes happen when turning left in junctions, which suggests riders are more careful there than other drivers."),
("You turn left on a motorcycle. Who is the most common other party in a crash?",
 "Drivers coming from behind", ["Pedestrians on the far side", "Cyclists ahead of you", "Buses pulling out of a stop"],
 "When a motorcyclist turns left, the other parties are mainly drivers coming from behind, then oncoming drivers the rider fails to give way to."),
("What is the most common kind of motorcycle crash in a roundabout?",
 "Hitting the central island", ["Hitting a cyclist on the exit", "Being hit from behind", "Hitting a pedestrian"],
 "The most common motorcycle crash in roundabouts is a single-vehicle crash where the rider loses control and hits the central island. Enter slowly."),
("You are already riding round a roundabout. What should you watch for at each entry?",
 "Drivers not giving way", ["Cars reversing out", "Trams turning left", "Lorries parking on the island"],
 "Quite a few crashes happen when a motorcyclist is in the roundabout and drivers entering do not hold back. Watch their speed and wheels."),
("In a roundabout with two lanes you move to the outer lane before your exit. Which rules apply?",
 "Those for changing lanes", ["You may cut straight across", "The inner lane must stop", "Those for merging in turn"],
 "Inside a roundabout you look and change lane just as on any road: mirrors, head check and a gap that is no danger or needless nuisance to others."),
("Which group of riders is often involved in crashes when going straight on through junctions?",
 "Young motorcyclists", ["Riders with sidecars", "Riders over 60", "Riders on the motorway"],
 "Quite a few accidents happen with young motorcyclists going straight on through junctions, often when an oncoming driver turns left in front of them."),
("You wait to turn left. A bus is coming towards you with a cyclist riding close beside it. What is the risk?",
 "You overlook the cyclist", ["The bus will stop for you", "The cyclist must give way", "The bus hides the lights"],
 "Vehicles that fill little of the picture are easily overlooked when they travel with larger ones. Look for cyclists and mopeds beside buses and lorries before you turn."),
("You ride into a pedestrian street (gågade) where riding is allowed. How fast should you go?",
 "Under about 15 km/h", ["Up to 30 km/h", "Up to 40 km/h", "As fast as cyclists there"],
 "In a pedestrian street riding must only be at very low speed, normally under 15 km/h, and you must not continue if people near you have not noticed you."),
("In a cycle street (cykelgade) where riding is allowed, what speed is normally the most?",
 "30 km/h", ["15 km/h", "40 km/h", "50 km/h"],
 "In a cycle street speed must suit the others there and is normally at most 30 km/h. Show special care and do not hold others up needlessly."),
("In a play street (opholds- og legeområde), which motorcycle may be parked only in marked spaces?",
 "One with more than two wheels", ["One with a passenger seat", "Any motorcycle over 125 cm³", "Only a motorcycle with a trailer"],
 "In a play street and a pedestrian street, a motorcycle with more than two wheels may only be parked in the specially marked spaces."),
("A lane arrow is painted next to the U of the word BUS. Who must follow the arrow?",
 "Buses only", ["All motor vehicles", "Motorcycles and buses", "Cyclists only"],
 "A lane arrow placed close to the U in BUS applies only to buses."),
]
